This is COMPKEY.EXE V1.10ft.  ( Will this ever end ! )

I converted all the code so that I could run it in 32 bit protected mode
and after 2 hours of debugging, I may have found the problem.

It would appear that under certain conditions, if you enter an invalid
plu and press enter, 12 bytes at address 0000:0008 will be overwritten
and bang go your interrupt vectors !

The only reason this happens on your machine is due to a typo in the test
script.  On the key before the "CANS" key, I should have put PLU 318 
but I put in 3180 which doesn't exist - POP!

None of my previous tests entered an invalid PLU.

So the moral of this story is :-

      People should NEVER enter invalid PLU's.



I have included GENKEYS.EXE if you need to run it I will talk you through
it's use.


